'' 'cint<n>( x )' and 'cuint<n>( x )' are ALIASES for the width-specific conversions,
'' not conversions of their own -- measured with '#print typeof': 'cint<16>( 1 )' is
'' SHORT and 'cuint<8>( 1 )' is UBYTE, the same table the sized TYPE spellings use.
''
'' Nothing parsed them: 'cint<32>( -1 )' came out as '(cint < 32) > (-1)', two
'' comparisons over an unbound name. numbers/integer_n.bas is written entirely in terms
'' of them.
''
'' The rewrite only fires on the whole '< n >' shape, so a bare 'cint' followed by a
'' comparison parses as it always did.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/sized-conv.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/sized-conv.out
